{"id": "l1", "act": "look", "body": "Fictional person G, counsel for the insured (stipulated stance). The site work was excavation of a pit, drainage, and concrete block retaining walls with a wood cap, the walls to prevent erosion and collapse (lines 80-90). The insured says the district court ignored the plain meaning of undefined terms like \"landscaping\" (lines 395-399), and the opinion reports that he claims the site work is \"landscaping\" (lines 484-488). The Court took the term as ambiguous and construed it in his favour (lines 440-446).", "author": "G (fictional counsel for the insured)", "kind": "person", "value": null, "object": null, "absent": null, "sources": ["sources/snell-v-united-specialty-2024.txt, lines 80-90", "sources/snell-v-united-specialty-2024.txt, lines 395-399", "sources/snell-v-united-specialty-2024.txt, lines 440-446", "sources/snell-v-united-specialty-2024.txt, lines 484-488"], "rests": ["g3 (for A):l1", "g3 (for A):l2"], "answers": [], "about": null, "narrows": null, "withdraws": null, "reason": null, "procedure": null, "via": null, "log": "G (fictional counsel for the insured)", "prev": null, "rest_hashes": ["d89a74d96805f7c3acddff9c57de4796fe7a74b1618790b29441bdcde3a0cfb3", "de08cf689c0580fada77ee5c1db6ebb3b35ea9e26de1cacb31faef4c7f81e992"], "hash": "df3ab3f95717abf09c87f700489a2697ec2a6ded56869bc11ee93bcfa74970da", "sig": "95c1dee7ca96bb41efe5c94a3735fbb58693917bc1404b13a38892e59d2eff8bfb3c865d64b5f6f678967af30b0ca9ad01604d014f75e5a5f178756d32fd6f0d"}
